WHAT THIS IS

The source of this application is published so it can be read, inspected and
audited by anyone. It is not, at present, open-source software: publishing the
source and granting the right to reuse it are two different things, and only
the first has been done so far.

This notice exists because a public repository with no licence at all is
ambiguous by omission — it reads as an oversight, while defaulting in law to
"all rights reserved". The position below is deliberate, not an oversight.

WHAT YOU MAY DO

  1. Read, study and inspect this source code, in full, for any purpose.
  2. Download a released build and use it, including for your own paid work.
     No fee is charged and none is currently planned.
  3. Build this source yourself and run the result on machines you control.
  4. Quote excerpts with attribution — in a review, an article, a bug report,
     a discussion of how it works.

WHAT IS NOT GRANTED YET

  1. Redistributing this software, in source or built form, to others.
  2. Publishing modified versions or derivative works.
  3. Selling it, bundling it into a paid product, or offering it as a service.
  4. Sublicensing any of the above to anyone else.

"Not granted yet" is meant literally. These terms may be relaxed later, and
that is the likely direction. If they are, the change applies from the version
it is published with — anything released under more permissive terms stays
under them permanently, because that cannot be taken back.

If you want to do something in the second list, ask:
inprincipio.project@gmail.com. A plain question gets a plain answer.

THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

Parts of this application come from other people's work and keep their own
licences, which are more permissive than this one and are not narrowed by it.
The writing editor is based on Loomdraft (MIT). Every such component and its
terms are listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md; that file governs those parts.

The AI command-line tools this application drives — Claude Code, Codex,
Cursor, OpenCode — are not included, not redistributed, and not covered here.
Each is installed and paid for by the person using it, under its own terms.

NO WARRANTY

This software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied, including but not limited to the warranties of merchantability,
fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. In no event shall the
author be liable for any claim, damages or other liability, whether in an
action of contract, tort or otherwise, arising from, out of or in connection
with the software or the use or other dealings in the software.

Note: this is a plain-language licence written for a small personal project,
not a standard OSI-approved one. GitHub will therefore show the licence of
this repository as unrecognised, which is expected and correct — it is not
an open-source licence, and labelling it as one would be the actual error.
